## Leaving the template

This repository is maintained by the template it came from: a scheduled workflow runs
`copier update` and opens a pull request when the template changes. If you would rather keep
what you have and stop syncing:

```bash
just eject                # print what would change
just eject -- --yes       # apply
```

That removes the answers file, the sync workflow, the module health report and the ADR that
records generation-time module decisions, and drops the references to them in the justfile,
the git hooks, `.github/CODEOWNERS` and the ADR index. Everything else stays: the workflows, the
devcontainer, the docs, the settings and your own files. The ADR skeleton stays too, because
`docs/adr/README.md` tells you to copy it.

Prose is not rewritten for you — the script prints the files that still talk about the template
so you can edit them. Ejecting is one-way: with no answers file, `copier update` no longer runs.
